.TH MU2EDAQ-FILE-REAPER-API 7 "2026-09-11" "mu2edaq-file-reaper 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq-file-reaper-api \- REST API of the Mu2e DAQ file reaper (version 1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B http://\fIhost\fR:5004/api/v1/\fIresource\fR
.PP
.nf
curl -s http://mu2e-dl-01:5004/api/v1/state | python3 -m json.tool
curl -s -X POST -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\
     -d '{"reason": "calibration"}' http://mu2e-dl-01:5004/api/v1/areas/data-raw/pause
.fi
.SH AUTHENTICATION
Three mechanisms, checked in this order:
.TP
.B Bearer token
.IR "Authorization: Bearer rpr_..." .
Tokens are created on the
.B /tokens
page or with
.B POST /api/v1/tokens
and carry scopes
.BR read " < " operate " < " admin
(a higher scope implies the lower ones).  Only a PBKDF2 hash is stored; the
plaintext is shown once at creation.
.TP
.B Admin header
.IR "X-Admin-Token: <reaper.admin_token>"
grants the admin scope.  Intended for minting the first token.
.TP
.B Admin session
The browser's session cookie after
.BR "POST /login" .
Mutating requests made with a session must also send
.IR "X-CSRF-Token" ,
the value the page embeds.
.PP
GET endpoints need no authentication while
.B api.open_read
is true (default).  Every mutating call always needs one of the mechanisms
and is recorded in the history with
.I actor
set to
.IR token:<name> " or " ui:admin .
.SH ERRORS
Errors are JSON objects
.IR "{\[dq]error\[dq]: \[dq]message\[dq]}"
with status 400 (bad request), 401 (authentication required), 403 (scope or
CSRF), 404 (unknown area, entry, token or exclusion) or 409 (conflict, for
example a dry run while a scan is running).
.SH ENDPOINTS
Scope column: \- means none, R read, O operate, A admin.
.SS Liveness
.TP
.B GET /health \-
.IR status " (ok | degraded), " version ", " label ", " uptime_s ", " areas ", " scan_interval ", " dry_run ", " config_issues ", " database_ok ", " scheduler
(alive, stalled, tick_age_s, next_tick_in_s, busy).
.TP
.B GET /version \-
Name, version, label, api.
.TP
.B GET /whoami \-
Kind (token | session | admin_header | anonymous), name, scopes, actor of the
caller.
.SS Areas
.TP
.B GET /state R
Everything: summary counts, every area snapshot, scheduler health.
.TP
.B GET /areas R
Area snapshots and summary.
.TP
.B GET /areas/<name> R
One snapshot plus its configuration and
.I usage_history
(ts, used_pct from past scans).
.TP
.B POST /areas/<name>/pause O
Body
.IR "{\[dq]reason\[dq]}" .
Scans continue, nothing is acted on.
.TP
.B POST /areas/<name>/resume O
.TP
.B POST /areas/<name>/rescan O
Request an immediate scan.
.TP
.B POST /areas/<name>/disable A
No scans until enabled.
.TP
.B POST /areas/<name>/enable A
.TP
.B POST /dry-run/<name> O
Run one scan now in dry-run mode on the request thread; returns
.I report
(scan_id, outcome, passes, acted, bytes_freed) and the resulting snapshot.
409 while a scan of that area is running.
.SS Queues
.TP
.B GET /queues R
Parameters
.IR area ", " kind " (compress | delete), " status .
Returns
.IR totals " and " entries ,
each with id, path, rel, name, size, size_str, atime, mtime, key_ts, owner,
group, mode, queue, tier, policy, status, reason, area, area_label.
.TP
.B GET /queues/<id> R
One entry by id (dev:ino) or path.
.SS Exclusions
.TP
.B GET /exclusions R
Parameters
.IR area ", " all .
.TP
.B POST /exclusions O
Body
.IR pattern " (or " path "), " area " (null = every area), " kind " (path | glob), " reason ", " expires_in " (duration) or " expires_at .
201 with the stored rule.
.TP
.B DELETE /exclusions/<id> O
Deactivates the rule.
.SS History
.TP
.B GET /history R
Parameters
.IR area ", " path " (glob), " type " (comma-separated event types), " tier ", " scan_id ", " since ", " until " (ISO-8601 or relative such as 24h), " limit " (default 100), " offset ", " order " (desc | asc), " format " (json | csv)."
Returns
.IR total ", " events .
Each event: id, ts, area, event_type, path, tier, policy, queue, outcome,
reason, size_bytes, bytes_freed, duration_s, used_pct_before, used_pct_after,
count, actor, scan_id, detail.
.TP
.B GET /history/types R
The event type vocabulary.
.SS Notifications
.TP
.B GET /notifications R
Channels (name, enabled, min_severity, disabled_reason, last_sent), recent
log rows, sent and failed counters.
.TP
.B POST /notifications/test A
Body
.IR channel " (optional), " severity ", " title ", " message .
.SS Tokens
.TP
.B GET /tokens A
Parameter
.IR all .
Never includes hashes or plaintext.
.TP
.B POST /tokens A
Body
.IR name ", " scopes " (list or comma string), " expires_in .
201 with
.I token
(plaintext, once) and
.IR record .
.TP
.B DELETE /tokens/<id> A
Revoke.
.SS Configuration
.TP
.B GET /config R
Settings in effect (secrets redacted), parsed areas, issues, notification
configuration.
.SH AREA SNAPSHOT
Every snapshot carries exactly these keys:
name, path, real_path, label, enabled, dry_run, state (GOOD WARNING CRITICAL
FULL PAUSED DISABLED UNKNOWN MISSING), rank, paused, paused_reason,
paused_by, paused_at, disabled, disabled_reason, disabled_by, disabled_at,
usage (total used free used_pct ts), usage_str, atime_mode, tiers (per tier:
threshold trigger stop policy min_age active low_water high_water
bytes_to_stop bytes_to_stop_str), active_tiers, selected_tier, scan (scan_id
pass_no started finished duration_s outcome reason acted bytes_freed
bytes_freed_str files_seen), queues (compress and delete: total shown
entries), progress (acting current_path acted remaining bytes_freed),
reject_counts, scan_errors, warnings, config_errors, last_scan_at,
next_scan_in_s.
.SH EVENT TYPES
scan_start, scan_end, scan_abort, tier_activate, tier_deactivate, queue_add,
queue_remove, action_delete, action_compress, action_failed,
policy_insufficient, space_not_reclaimed, exclusion_add, exclusion_remove,
area_pause, area_resume, area_disable, area_enable, notification_sent,
token_create, token_revoke, maintenance.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq-file-reaper (1),
.BR mu2edaq-reaper (1),
